insert into public.posts (id, campaign_id, theme, position, body, linkedin_url, status, scheduled_at, posted_at)
values ('cde5ace7-9557-4ac1-ab66-b0c2704ddd66', 'f34a2607-06a3-4c4b-8e3d-2315bc92afb5', 'A book (or podcast) that recently shifted my perspective', 18, 'Recently, I picked up The Grand Chessboard by Zbigniew Brzezinski.

On the surface, it’s a book about geopolitics and U.S. strategy in the 1990s.
But for me, the real insight went beyond politics - it was about perspective.

The book reminded me that no decision exists in isolation.
Every move, whether in global politics or in business, has ripple effects across a much larger “board.”

And if you want to build something sustainable, you need to understand both the immediate step and the wider strategy.

At CipherCross, this shifted how I think about our company’s position in the world.
Wellness technology doesn’t live in a vacuum - it’s influenced by social trends, policy changes, and economic shifts.

Staying “in tune” with the bigger picture is just as important as perfecting the next product feature.

My key takeaway:
➡️ Leaders need to balance micro execution with macro awareness.
That’s where resilience is built.

What book or podcast recently shifted your perspective?

Leadership #Strategy #Wellness #CipherCross', 'https://www.linkedin.com/posts/mykyta-shevchenko-ciphercross-wellness_leadership-strategy-wellness-activity-7442480422464253952-bu4R?utm_source=share&utm_medium=member_desktop&rcm=ACoAACKi8XsB9WBoWK1z6g7nRgrBaW3-4QoyJT8', 'posted', '2026-03-25T07:00:00Z', '2026-03-25T07:00:00Z');
insert into public.post_stats (post_id, views, likes, comments, recorded_at)
values ('cde5ace7-9557-4ac1-ab66-b0c2704ddd66', 74, 1, 0, '2026-06-02T12:00:00Z');
insert into public.posts (id, campaign_id, theme, position, body, linkedin_url, status, scheduled_at, posted_at)
values ('0be6f079-6051-4f27-b879-a996598ce94f', 'f34a2607-06a3-4c4b-8e3d-2315bc92afb5', 'Mental health is a marathon, not a sprint', 19, 'I’ve noticed something in both business and life:
We love quick fixes.
A single retreat.
One therapy session.
A motivational quote.

But real mental health doesn’t come from shortcuts.
It’s not a sprint - it’s a marathon.

For me, the difference became clear when I finally allowed myself to rest after years of nonstop work.
I realized that recharging isn’t about one moment - it’s about building long-term systems that support you consistently.

Sometimes that system is a 3–5 hour hike in nature, where ideas start flowing and my mind clears.
Other times, it’s something small, like giving myself permission to celebrate a task with a treat or even 30 minutes of Instagram scrolling.

It’s not about the length of the activity - it’s about recognizing what your mind and body need at that moment.

At CipherCross, this is also how we approach wellness technology: not as a one-off “solution,” but as an ongoing journey.
Systems, habits, and supportive structures matter far more than quick wins.

Mental health is not a checkbox.
It’s a practice you commit to every day.

What does your “marathon” of mental health look like?', 'https://www.linkedin.com/posts/mykyta-shevchenko-ciphercross-wellness_ive-noticed-something-in-both-business-and-activity-7442835255415390208-b3mZ?utm_source=share&utm_medium=member_desktop&rcm=ACoAACKi8XsB9WBoWK1z6g7nRgrBaW3-4QoyJT8', 'posted', '2026-03-26T06:30:00Z', '2026-03-26T06:30:00Z');
insert into public.post_stats (post_id, views, likes, comments, recorded_at)
values ('0be6f079-6051-4f27-b879-a996598ce94f', 91, 2, 0, '2026-06-02T12:00:00Z');
insert into public.posts (id, campaign_id, theme, position, body, linkedin_url, status, scheduled_at, posted_at)
values ('fd32e3ab-5944-4b59-917b-5aabee0552c1', 'f34a2607-06a3-4c4b-8e3d-2315bc92afb5', 'Staying hungry - not for money, but for experiences', 20, 'Many people tie ambition to money.
The idea is: if you want to succeed, you need to stay hungry - for wealth, titles, recognition.

But I’ve learned that this kind of hunger rarely leads to fulfillment.

The mindset that has brought me the most growth - in business and in life - is different: staying hungry for experiences.

Because life is not a straight line toward a bank account balance.
It’s a mosaic of moments, challenges, lessons, and perspectives.

For me, this means:

→ Saying yes to new adventures, even when they’re outside my comfort zone.
→ Approaching cultures, people, and ideas with curiosity instead of judgment.
→ Treating every experience as a way to expand not just my knowledge, but my empathy.

This mindset directly shapes how we build at CipherCross, too.

Creating wellness apps isn’t just about scaling technology - it’s about embracing the multipolarity of human lives, meeting people where they are, and learning from every interaction.

When you stay hungry for experiences, you stop chasing growth just in numbers.
You start creating growth that actually matters.

 What are you currently “hungry” for - money, recognition, or experiences?

no photo, because it is “reflection” post', 'https://www.linkedin.com/posts/mykyta-shevchenko-ciphercross-wellness_many-people-tie-ambition-to-money-the-idea-activity-7444262151915028480-6Jnw?utm_source=share&utm_medium=member_desktop&rcm=ACoAACKi8XsB9WBoWK1z6g7nRgrBaW3-4QoyJT8', 'posted', '2026-03-30T06:00:00Z', '2026-03-30T06:00:00Z');
