insert into public.posts (id, campaign_id, theme, position, body, linkedin_url, status, scheduled_at, posted_at)
values ('13124032-91bb-4b34-bd56-b8b6b48b39e3', 'f34a2607-06a3-4c4b-8e3d-2315bc92afb5', 'Product building & working with users', 27, 'There’s something magical about that first moment of real feedback.
When someone uses the product you helped bring to life - and it clicks.

Not because the tech is perfect.
Not because the design is flawless.
But because it solves a real problem for a real person.

That’s the moment I work for.
Every time.

Throughout my journey - as a builder, as a founder, as a curious human - I’ve always been drawn to ideas.
Not just my own, but other people’s.
The raw, messy, inspiring, world-changing kind.

And the real magic for me happens when those ideas finally take shape.

→ When someone who had a dream on a piece of paper sees it turn into a working product.
→  When their internal vision becomes external reality.
→ When real users interact with something that once only existed in their imagination.

That’s the kind of impact I want to make.
Not just by building - but by enabling others to build.

The tools are there.
The opportunities are endless.
And the only limit, most of the time, is that people don’t know where to start — or don’t believe they can.

That’s where I want to help.

We need more ideas turned into action.
More people believe in their ability to create.
And more of us are showing up not just to build for, but to build with.

So if you’re sitting on a product idea, unsure where to go next - or just want to bring something new into the world:

Let’s talk.

Sometimes, all it takes is one real conversation to move things forward.

 What’s the idea you’ve been holding onto?', 'https://www.linkedin.com/posts/mykyta-shevchenko-ciphercross-wellness_theres-a-specific-moment-in-product-work-activity-7449350714432090112-Z5Lt?utm_source=share&utm_medium=member_desktop&rcm=ACoAACKi8XsB9WBoWK1z6g7nRgrBaW3-4QoyJT8', 'posted', '2026-04-14T07:00:00Z', '2026-04-14T07:00:00Z');
