insert into public.posts (id, campaign_id, theme, position, body, linkedin_url, status, scheduled_at, posted_at)
values ('8fb484d5-8706-4ab1-ab9e-a646c324da96', 'f34a2607-06a3-4c4b-8e3d-2315bc92afb5', 'How to build trust in health tech', 31, 'Wellness tech isn’t about data. It’s about feeling understood.

Most apps in health and wellness are built to track.

Steps.
Calories.
Sleep.

But numbers alone don’t make people feel better.
What actually makes a difference is when technology understands context and supports you like a human would.

At CipherCross, we design wellness products around one simple idea:
Technology should help people build healthier lives, not just collect their signals.

That means:

- Collecting only the minimum viable data, not everything we can, but only what we need to help.
- Making consent obvious, not hidden in settings.
- Keeping sensitive logic on-device whenever possible, so raw health signals stay with the user.
- Turning data into personalized, supportive journeys, not dashboards that leave people overwhelmed.

This approach isn’t the fastest way to build products, but it’s the only way to build trust.

And trust is the foundation of long-term impact in wellness tech.

If you’re building in health, wellness, or behavior change, how do you think tech can better support people, not just measure them?

(впевнена, що не використовували це фото, але в разі чого, то тегнете)', 'https://www.linkedin.com/posts/mykyta-shevchenko-ciphercross-wellness_trust-in-healthtech-saas-activity-7452963223231709184-4r0f?utm_source=share&utm_medium=member_desktop&rcm=ACoAACKi8XsB9WBoWK1z6g7nRgrBaW3-4QoyJT8', 'posted', '2026-04-23T06:15:00Z', '2026-04-23T06:15:00Z');
insert into public.post_stats (post_id, views, likes, comments, recorded_at)
