insert into public.posts (id, campaign_id, theme, position, body, linkedin_url, status, scheduled_at, posted_at)
values ('b54626ca-7fd4-4eaa-8c22-3922ea8abc15', '62b02c62-e03e-4c72-9fc7-058c87b3d847', 'The silent power of security-by-design', 4, 'Format: Behind-the-scenes / Process deep dive Type: Tech / Trust Hook:  Most users won’t notice a solid security architecture. And that’s exactly the point.  Body idea: Explain how CipherCross bakes security into the foundation, not as a “patch” later on. Briefly touch on encryption, trusted tools, regulations, and client reassurance. Include a quote from the dev/infra team.  CTA: → Building secure-by-default wellness platforms: ciphercross.com', null, 'posted', '2025-08-27T08:00:00Z', '2025-08-27T08:00:00Z');
insert into public.posts (id, campaign_id, theme, position, body, linkedin_url, status, scheduled_at, posted_at)
values ('9bbf440d-0174-48b4-a2cf-ce724549c76d', '62b02c62-e03e-4c72-9fc7-058c87b3d847', 'AI + empathy: the new wave of wellness apps', 5, 'Published

AI + empathy: the new wave of wellness apps!

We’re witnessing a new chapter in digital wellness - one driven by language models that can analyze mood, spot behavioral patterns, and suggest resources instantly. Large Language Models (LLMs) have made it possible to create support that feels truly personal, any time you need it.

But here’s the challenge: Real care isn’t just about fast answers or advanced algorithms, genuine support needs heart.

At CipherCross, we believe empathy is the missing ingredient. Our vision is clear: for AI-powered wellness tools to help users thrive, they must understand more than symptoms - they must feel the nuance of a bad day, the hesitation in a message, the hope behind a question.

How do we build “empathetic UX”?
→ We train our AI to recognize not just requests, but emotion and context.
→ Our team consults with real therapists and users to map out authentic support journeys.
→ Every suggested resource, prompt, or reply is filtered through the lens of “What would a caring human say here?”

For example: When a user checks in with our app after a tough night, the response isn’t a generic “how can I help?” - but a personalized note that reflects understanding, offers gentle next steps, and, when appropriate, recommends reaching out to a real professional.

It’s tech that listens - and responds - with heart.

Because the future of wellness isn’t just smart, but sincerely human.

→ Discover how we combine AI and emotional intelligence: ciphercross.com

WellnessTech #MentalHealth #AI #Empathy #UX #TechForGood #CipherCross #EmotionalIntelligence', null, 'posted', '2025-09-02T08:45:00Z', '2025-09-02T08:45:00Z');
insert into public.posts (id, campaign_id, theme, position, body, linkedin_url, status, scheduled_at, posted_at)
values ('9ff6cca9-b21b-4a69-b4f2-091446d3613d', '62b02c62-e03e-4c72-9fc7-058c87b3d847', ': Thriving in an Over-Digitized World', 6, 'Format: Long-form expert post with practical tips Type: Expertise / Thought Leadership Hook: "In a world where our phones never stop buzzing, how do we help our minds find silence?" Body Idea: The post opens with a relatable scenario: back-to-back notifications, endless scrolling, mental fatigue. Then transitions into CipherCross’s belief that wellness technology should give people more peace, not less. Share 3 actionable micro-habits for digital balance, followed by how CipherCross builds apps to encourage focus, mental clarity, and healthier living — from mindfulness reminders to intentional “screen break” prompts. CTA: "How do you personally create digital quiet in your day? Let’s share ideas."', 'https://www.linkedin.com/feed/update/urn:li:activity:7442843168993226752', 'posted', '2026-03-26T07:00:00Z', '2026-03-26T07:00:00Z');
