insert into public.posts (id, campaign_id, theme, position, body, linkedin_url, status, scheduled_at, posted_at)
values ('e9a0e6b9-8886-4cfa-afd6-d1c43110250d', '62b02c62-e03e-4c72-9fc7-058c87b3d847', 'The Hidden Layers of a Mental-Health App', 25, 'Why We Start with Empathy?

Too many apps are built around features,
 settings, and routines that assume
 Everyone feels their best at all times.

But what about the moments
 You can’t predict - the ones that don’t fit on a product roadmap?
 That’s where empathy comes in.

1. Real Users, Real Stories:
 We listen to user experiences,
 from stressful deadlines to peaceful routines,
 to shape every step of the journey.

2. Accessibility Always:
 Support and relief should be a tap away,
 never hidden behind logins or complicated flows.

4. Continuous Care:
 We design for every context - late nights,
 anxious afternoons,
 or mindful mornings - because mental health happens 24/7.

How Empathy Shapes Our App

1. Onboarding that Listens:
 Our first question isn’t about your goals—it’s about how you’re feeling right now.

2. Check-Ins, Not Checklists:
 We offer gentle, optional daily check-ins.
 No pressure.
 Just presence, right when you need it.

3. Personalized Rituals:
 You can set up routines for your unique life—whether that’s five minutes before a meeting or ten minutes before bed.

4. Instant Support:
 From emergency calming tools to grounding techniques,
 help should never be out of reach in those “invisible” struggle moments.

The User Journey We Imagine:

→ Midnight, can’t sleep:
 One tap and you’re in a safe,
 non-judgmental space - no login walls, no pop-up offers.

→ Workday stress:
 Subtle, supportive reminders appear
 only if you want them - respecting your boundaries,
 not cluttering your focus.

→ Morning calm:
 Rituals support mindful starts,
 customized to be as quiet or as active as you need.

Building the mental health app we all deserve
 means designing for our most human moments.

At CipherCross, empathy leads the way,
So wellness becomes a companion - not just an app on your phone.

What would your perfect mental health journey look like?
 Share your thoughts - I’d love to hear how technology could support you, too.

WellnessTech #UserExperience #MentalHealth #CustomerSuccess #EmpathyInTech #CipherCross', 'https://www.linkedin.com/feed/update/urn:li:activity:7453102947208540160', 'posted', '2026-04-23T15:30:00Z', '2026-04-23T15:30:00Z');
