insert into public.posts (id, campaign_id, theme, position, body, linkedin_url, status, scheduled_at, posted_at)
values ('49965d09-df3e-4e24-aa90-662bc266de76', '562570de-9832-4997-937e-45a0b88649fd', 'The Hidden Challenge in Customer Success', 11, 'Customer Success isn’t just about solving problems.
It’s about predicting them before they appear - and that’s the hardest part.

Customer Success is more than just a reactive role.
It''s a proactive stance that is integral to the success of our clients and our business.
A client comes with an issue → you fix it → they’re happy again.

But real Customer Success happens long before the first ticket is raised.
It’s in the moments when you:
 → Notice when you notice subtle changes in usage patterns in the data, which could indicate a potential issue.
 → Catch a pattern in customer behavior that signals frustration
 → Sense hesitation in a client’s tone before they even mention a concern

Because by the time a problem becomes visible, it’s already slowing down adoption, trust, and results.

The real challenge lies in balancing empathy with foresight.
You need to deeply understand what customers are saying, and also what they might not be saying but feeling.
You need to listen deeply to what customers say - but also read between the lines of what they don’t.

That’s why the best CS leaders aren’t just problem-solvers. They’re proactive strategists. They design experiences where obstacles never even reach the client.

It’s not easy, and we understand the challenges you face in your role. But it''s these challenges that make our work in Customer Success so rewarding.
It’s not apparent.
But it’s what turns “good support” into a true partnership.

 Curious to hear from others in Customer Success - how do you anticipate client needs before they even surface?', null, 'generated', null, null);
