values ('e443f386-2226-4cdd-8097-f61ea22d392a', '17f1612e-5938-415a-b812-8b00dc905d0f', 'How I Unplug to Reconnect', 9, 'Format: Storytelling + personal photo (travel, nature, or weekend activity)  Type: Personal  Hook: "Paradoxically, my best work ideas don’t come at work. They come when I unplug — walking in nature, exploring new places, or just being offline."  Angle: Personal wellness habit that shapes creativity and resilience. Ties back subtly to wellness tech & CipherCross values.', null, 'approved', null, null);
insert into public.posts (id, campaign_id, theme, position, body, linkedin_url, status, scheduled_at, posted_at)
values ('304f6bf6-d5b3-4a2c-8a79-bd6a523eb3cf', '17f1612e-5938-415a-b812-8b00dc905d0f', 'The Metrics That Matter Most in Customer Success', 10, 'The Metrics That Matter Most in Customer Success

Not every metric tells the truth.
In customer success, the wrong numbers can make you feel ‘successful’,
while customers are quietly slipping away.

I’ve seen it happen many times.
Teams celebrate high NPS or a growing number of logins…
But beneath the surface, customers are disengaging.

So, what really matters?

Here are the 3 metrics I trust most when it comes to building lasting success with customers:

1. Engagement depth - not just if customers log in, but how they use the product. Are they reaching meaningful outcomes or just clicking around?

2. Retention & expansion - renewals, upsells, and expansions are the clearest signals that customers see long-term value.

3. Customer well-being - harder to measure, but crucial. Regular health checks, sentiment analysis, and even honest conversations can reveal risks before numbers do.

Vanity metrics may look good on a slide,
but these three tell the real story.

At CipherCross, we believe customer success isn’t about chasing numbers - it’s about tracking the right ones, so we can create real value, stronger partnerships, and more resilient growth.

What metrics do you believe reveal the truth about customer success?', null, 'approved', null, null);
